  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Barfoed&rsquo;s test is used for distinguishing monosaccharides from reducing disaccharides. Monosaccharides usually react in about <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;minute while the reducing disaccharides take much longer time between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn></math>&nbsp;minutes to react with the reagent. Brick red color is obtained in this test which is due to formation of cuprous oxide</p><p>Barfoed&#39;s test is basically used for detecting the presence of monosaccharides.</p>",
